\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Peak resident set (GB) and the factor by which \textsc  {Ptctlmc}{} undercuts each baseline. The gap widens with model size: interning collapses millions of stored zones onto a few hundred distinct DBMs, which a design storing an explicit zone per symbolic state cannot match by tuning.}}{11}{table.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:mem}{{3}{11}{Peak resident set (GB) and the factor by which \tool {} undercuts each baseline. The gap widens with model size: interning collapses millions of stored zones onto a few hundred distinct DBMs, which a design storing an explicit zone per symbolic state cannot match by tuning}{table.caption.11}{}}
